=== CO4 TASK 3: OUTPATIENT CABLING AUDIT, DEVICES & BILL OF MATERIALS ===
3.1 TIA/EIA-568 Audit (Max 90 m Permanent Link, 100 m Channel):
  - Consulting rooms (35-80 m)     |  80 m | PASS (<90m)           | Use: Cat6 UTP (or Cat6A for 10G future)
  - Pharmacy (96 m)                |  96 m | FAIL (>90m perm link!) | Use: Multimode Fibre OM3/OM4 (zero distance margin left on copper)
  - Waiting-hall APs (60 m)        |  60 m | PASS (<90m)           | Use: Cat6A UTP (supports PoE+ & multi-gig Wi-Fi 6)
  - Link to main building (420 m)  | 420 m | FAIL (4.2x > 100m!)   | Use: OS2 Single-mode Fibre (420m > 10G OM3/OM4 300-400m limit)

Mixed T568A/T568B Patch Cables:
  - Created: Crossover cables (TX pairs 1-2 & 3-6 swapped).
  - Modern switches: Still work seamlessly due to Auto-MDIX (IEEE 802.3ab), though standardising on T568B is best.

3.2 Device Selection & Domain Counts (Outpatient Block):
  - Chosen: L2 PoE+ Access Switches + Wi-Fi 6 APs + L3 Core Switch/Router + Stateful Firewall (NO hubs).
  - Collision Domains : 1 per active switch port + 1 per wireless cell (eliminates shared hub collisions).
  - Broadcast Domains : 4 VLANs (Consulting, Pharmacy, Guest Wi-Fi, Management) terminated at L3 Switch/Router.

3.3 Bill of Materials (Outpatient Block, with 10% spare cable):
  - L2 Managed PoE+ 24-port Switch               | Qty: 2                  | 48 access + 4 SFP+ ports
  - Wi-Fi 6 Ceiling Access Points                | Qty: 4                  | 802.11ax dual-band
  - Cat6 / Cat6A UTP Cable (incl. 10% spare)     | Qty: 900 m (815 m + 10%) | RJ45 Cat6 plugs + keystone jacks
  - OM4 Multimode Fibre (incl. 10% spare)        | Qty: 106 m (96 m + 10%) | LC-LC duplex connectors
  - OS2 Single-mode Fibre (incl. 10% spare)      | Qty: 462 m (420 m + 10%) | LC-LC + SFP-10G-LR transceivers
  - 12U Wall/Floor Telecom Rack + Patch Panel + UPS | Qty: 1                  | 24-port Cat6 patch panel + LIU

3.4 T568B Pinout Colour Order (Pins 1 to 8):
  1: White-Orange | 2: Orange | 3: White-Green | 4: Blue | 5: White-Blue | 6: Green | 7: White-Brown | 8: Brown

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: 420 m Multimode Fibre vs Cat6A + Mid-Span Switch ---
  - Multimode/Single-mode Fibre : Single passive dielectric run (up to 550m-10km), zero mid-span power, immune to lightning/EMI.
  - Cat6A + Mid-span Switch     : Needs 4-5 segments/switches (<100m each) or 1 switch at 210m STILL exceeds 100m on each side!
    (To bridge 420m with 100m copper segments actually requires FOUR active mid-span switches + UPS + outdoor enclosures + surge arrestors!)
